Description: Separate host-account glob oracles from fixed-provider libc checks
Author: Peios maintainers
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-16

The host shell can resolve the Debian build user from /etc/passwd while the
Peios libc under test intentionally cannot. Under an explicit test-only flag,
omit only these host-account comparisons. The recipe independently requires
positive, escaped and missing-name glob tests against its Peios NSS fixture.
All filesystem-pattern and HOME-based cases remain unchanged.

--- a/posix/globtest.sh
+++ b/posix/globtest.sh
@@ -458,6 +458,12 @@
   fi
 fi
 
+# Peios libc uses its authority provider, not the host shell's passwd source.
+# Named-user cases run separately with a controlled Peios provider. Preserve
+# every non-account glob case in this script in the accountless build root.
+if test "${PEIOS_ACCOUNTLESS_GLOB_TEST:-0}" = 1; then
+  echo 'UNSUPPORTED: host-account tilde oracle; covered by staged Peios provider'
+else
 # Test tilde expansion with username
 failed=0
 ${test_program_prefix} \
@@ -471,6 +477,8 @@
   else
     echo "Tilde3 test could not be run" >> $logfile
   fi
+fi
+
 fi
 
 # Tilde expansion shouldn't match a file
@@ -775,7 +783,7 @@
